  "notes": "Round 1 -- run BEFORE the baseline window opens, on the pre-study set: 50 finished orders held from June 19-26 production, salted with the week's known rejects and borderline cases (15 of 50 questionable) so the judgment actually gets exercised -- 50 random orders at an ~9% reject rate would test almost nothing. Tessa Nguyen (rater A) and Omar Haddad (rater B) judged every order independently against the four checks, same desk, same lamp, order sheets swapped so neither saw the other's calls. Disagreements clustered exactly where the operational definition was soft: what counts as 'smudge' versus acceptable ink variation (5 of 7 splits), and whether a just-at-2mm trim is a fail (2 of 7). Engine verdict below: kappa in the marginal band -- proceed is not licensed; fix the definitions and re-run.",
